e filters differ from their defaults.\n6. List header: 'Catalog · <shown> of <total>' with the total from `catalog.counts` (files + wiki + modules), replacing the 'Catalog is limited. Search for more results.' banner; 'Results · <n>' while searching.\n7. The selected list row is scrolled into view when the selection changes (for example from the graph).\n8. Explorer banners (protocol error, read error, snapshot mismatch) render above the OpenSpec view, not below it. The freshness banner reads as one sentence ('Graph is stale: <reason>'), not 'Graph stale. an untracked ...'.\n9. Carried over from the review of the navigation task: the Wiki empty state must not say 'No Wiki page matches' while a search is still running; `useExplorerNavigation.ts` restores the scroll of `.metaproject-node-body`, the old panel body class, and must point at the new panel body; keep a map of nodes already seen so that Back to a node shows its panel at once instead of waiting for its projection.\n\nIn metaproject.css: remove the rules the swap makes dead (`.metaproject-node-*`, `.metaproject-relations`, the old `.metaproject-graph*` rules), remove the `@media (max-width: 700px)` block (the window cannot be narrower than 720 px, so it never applies) and, where a narrow layout is needed, use a container query on the explorer as `.composer` does elsewhere in the app. The three columns are list, content, panel. At the minimum window (720x480, a 660 px wide host) with the panel closed and no warning banner at least 140 px of graph height must be visible without scrolling (AC20); the orchestrator measures this in a browser.\n\nTests (MetaprojectView.dom.test.tsx): update what the swap changes (the Wiki tab must be activated before 'Open in Wiki'; the old relationship row texts are gone) and add tests for AC17. cytoscape cannot create a canvas under happy-dom; `RelationshipGraph` has a test-only `createCytoscape` prop (see RelationshipGraph.dom.test.tsx for the headless factory) — give the explor